From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_SSBO_SIZE_CAP=1: a word past 256 MiB after a storage buffer pointer is not a size (viejunerd/Eglantine-PS5- v1.219.029, patch 0082); off by default

Port of viejunerd's 0082-implausible-storage-buffer-size-word.patch (release v1.219.029,
commit 15cde68e7): StorageBufferBinding took the word after an SSBO pointer as the buffer's size
whenever it fit the mapping. At Ocarina of Time's Kokiri Forest load that word is the float 1.0
(0x3F800000) inside a larger mapping, so a 1,065,418,752-byte buffer was asked for and the
session ended with VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY while hundreds of MiB were free. With the
switch such a word is bound as a bare pointer (up to 8 MiB, cut at the mapping's end) and the
first 16 are logged as 'Storage buffer size word ... is not a size'.

Upstream's change is unconditional. Here it sits behind a switch, merged by hand into our
version of the function (EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_PROBECLAMP and the table pool sit between the two
upstream hunks); with the switch unset nothing changes.

diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
index 5feadd8..21aeb11 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
@@ -5607,6 +5607,14 @@ Binding BufferCache<P>::StorageBufferBinding(GPUVAddr ssbo_addr, u32 cbuf_index,
         }
     }
     const Binding binding = [&]() -> Binding {
+        // EDEN_UP_SSBO_SIZE_CAP=1 (viejunerd/Eglantine-PS5- v1.219.029, patch 0082): a word past
+        // 256 MiB after the pointer is another parameter, not a size. Ocarina of Time's Kokiri
+        // Forest load has the float 1.0 (0x3F800000) there inside a mapping larger than that,
+        // and the 1 GiB buffer it asked for ended the session out of device memory with
+        // hundreds of MiB still free. Such a word binds as a bare pointer (up to 8 MiB).
+        static const bool size_cap = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_SSBO_SIZE_CAP");
+        constexpr u32 MaxStorageSizeWord = static_cast<u32>(256_MiB);
+        bool bare_pointer = native_pointer;
         u32 size = [&]() {
             const u64 layout_size = static_cast<u64>(gpu_memory->GetMemoryLayoutSize(gpu_addr));
             // EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_PROBECLAMP=1 (Fritchii 8193f926fa, zortos293/Lichii#351): the
@@ -5647,9 +5655,19 @@ Binding BufferCache<P>::StorageBufferBinding(GPUVAddr ssbo_addr, u32 cbuf_index,
             const u32 packed_size = static_cast<u32>(next_qword);
             const bool next_qword_is_size = static_cast<u32>(next_qword >> 32) == 0 &&
                                             packed_size != 0 && packed_size <= memory_layout_size;
-            if (next_qword_is_size) {
+            if (next_qword_is_size && (!size_cap || packed_size <= MaxStorageSizeWord)) {
                 return packed_size;
             }
+            if (next_qword_is_size) {
+                bare_pointer = true;
+                static std::atomic<u32> reports{};
+                if (reports.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed) < 16) {
+                    LOG_WARNING(HW_GPU,
+                                "Storage buffer size word {:#x} at {:#x} is not a size: bound as a "
+                                "bare pointer",
+                                packed_size, ssbo_addr + 8);
+                }
+            }
             return (std::min)(memory_layout_size, static_cast<u32>(8_MiB));
         }();
         if (native_written_binding_mode != 0) {
@@ -5676,7 +5694,7 @@ Binding BufferCache<P>::StorageBufferBinding(GPUVAddr ssbo_addr, u32 cbuf_index,
                 }
             }
         }
-        if (native_pointer && size != 0) {
+        if (bare_pointer && size != 0) {
             // Stop where the mapping or its device range does: the binding is one device range, and
             // a written one isn't split into separate ranges without sparse sources.
             size = static_cast<u32>(gpu_memory->MaxContinuousRange(gpu_addr, size));
